Chapter: NetworkScopeOpen
  cites Net chapter HttpFetch

 The control half of the runtime network-scope experiment. This program
 declares Network.Write with no authority, so its grant is unscoped and
 every host is admitted -- an empty authority admits every host, which
 is what an unscoped grant means.

 It asks the gate about the same two URLs its twin network-scope-deny
 does, and both are admitted. The only difference between the two
 programs is a scope literal in the effect row. That is what makes the
 twin's refusal evidence of the scope and not of a broken gate: without
 this half, a denial and a bug are the same picture.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Network.Write] Nothing
  opening = act
    let a = if net-scope-admits "http://ok.host/path" then 10 else 0
    in let b = if net-scope-admits "http://evil.host/path" then 1 else 0
    in print-line-uni (show (a + b))
  end
